# Family A10: unsafe ring slot addressing (internal/queue under -tags
# iqmq_unsafe). See hack/bakeoff.sh.
#
# the benchmark configuration row A10 describes this family as "A1 on both builds":
# the arms are not two kinds inside one binary, they are the same nine queue
# kinds compiled twice, with bounds-checked slice indexing (slot.go) and with
# unsafe pointer arithmetic (slot_unsafe.go). The decision rule is the row's
# own -- "adopt unsafe only if > 10% gain; default pure Go" -- and it is a
# comparison BETWEEN this family's scorecard and A1's, kind by kind.
#
# So `bakeoff decide A10`'s own "winner" is which queue kind is fastest when
# the unsafe slot is compiled in, which is a fact about family A1, not a
# decision about A10. Nothing binds to it: AUTO_FILE=- because the unsafe path
# is selected by a build tag, not by an `Auto` constant, and A1's binding is
# the pure-Go one by default. Whoever writes ADR-021 computes the per-kind
# gain from benchmarks/reports/scorecards/{A1,A10}.json -- the two runs share
# every benchmark name, so the comparison is a join on the row name -- and
# applies the > 10% rule there.
#
# This exists as a declaration of its own because a re-run of A1 under the tag
# passes `-family A1` and would overwrite A1's scorecard with data from a
# different build, leaving ADR-014 rendered from unsafe numbers and ADR-021
# still reporting A10 unmeasured (hack/FOLLOWUPS.md).
PKG=./internal/queue
BENCH=BenchmarkMemory/Queue
REF=mutexring
AUTO_KEY=queue_unsafe
EXTRA_ARGS="-tags iqmq_unsafe"
AUTO_FILE=-
ADR=21
TITLE="Unsafe ring slot addressing: the A1 queue kinds compiled with pointer arithmetic (A10)"

#
# CRITERION is the benchmark configuration's decision column for this row, quoted.
# MATRIX is the IQMQ_BENCH_MATRIX grid the campaign measures the family at.
# DECIDED_AT names the benchmark-name segments the criterion is read at, and
# DECIDED_ON the metrics; `make bench-lint` lists the family's benchmarks at
# the declared grid and fails when a term or a metric is missing from the rows
# every kind has in common, which is the only data `bakeoff decide` reads.
CRITERION="adopt unsafe only if > 10% gain (ADR); default pure Go"
# MATRIX=full, and necessarily the same grid as A1: row A10's criterion is a
# per-kind comparison BETWEEN this scorecard and A1's, joined on the benchmark
# name , and two different grids share no names to join.
# `make bench-lint` refuses a mismatch.
MATRIX=full
DECIDED_AT="MPMC P=1 P=32 batch=1 batch=256 occupancy=0 occupancy=95 latency"
DECIDED_ON="ns/op allocs/op p99-ns"
PARTIAL_KINDS="spsc=single producer and single consumer by construction (queue.Kind.Modes = ModeSPSC); mpsc=single consumer by construction (queue.Kind.Modes = ModeSPSC|ModeMPSC), so no SPMC or MPMC row"
SHARES_ROOT="A1"
